# linux-client/prebuilt/ is a deliberate exception to the build-output
# ignore patterns below - it's the git-tracked fallback Linux client
# binary Install-Server.ps1 uses on machines without the Go toolchain
# installed, so a fresh checkout always has a real client to deploy.
output/
build/
dist/
tmp/
*.log
*.tmp
inventory-index.json

# Internal AI-assisted development scratch - useful locally while building a
# feature, not meant for a reader of the public repo.
docs/superpowers/
.superpowers/
.claude/skills/

# Fell behind the project during this branch's Linux-client/security work
# (still describes v0.21.3, no mention of the Linux client at all). Untracked
# until it gets a full rewrite against the current state - see the roadmap.
docs/project-specification.md

# Internal release-prep working notes - not meant for the public repo.
docs/pending-readme-updates.md

# Detailed release-by-release history, kept for local reference only -
# CHANGELOG.md is the public version history.
docs/project-history.md
